# text_id = 1270
# text = We know that HMRC recognises its power to use criminal investigation approaches to tackle the promotion and enabling of tax avoidance schemes , but in a letter the Financial Secretary sent me in January this year , he admitted that , since the formation of HMRC ’s fraud investigation service in 2016 , only 20 individuals have been convicted for offences relating to arrangements that have been promoted as tax avoidance .
